AB  - A cyber incident puts an organization’s management, security, and legal functions under joint time pressure, yet openly available training software exercises almost exclusively the technical layer. CSIRT-Sim closes this gap. It is an open-source simulator in which a small interdisciplinary team—Board, CISO, and Legal—jointly steers an organization through a time-compressed cyber crisis in which technical containment, business decisions, and statutory notification duties interact. Scenarios are declarative JSON interpreted by a deterministic engine, so exercises are versioned and repeatable; an auditable weighted-KPI scorer grades every session, while a large language model evaluates free-text actions, advises in-exercise, and writes the debrief. The bilingual scenario library spans banking and healthcare, including an AI-supply-chain incident family. CSIRT-Sim has been used in instructor-led cohorts and is openly available on GitHub.
