AB  - Intelligent Intrusion Detection Systems should be applied on heterogeneous security data while resistant against adversarial manipulation and operational drift. Yet, the prior work lacks Effective cross-source reasoning, produces hallucinatory outputs, and can be vulnerable against prompt injection and retrieval poisoning. In this paper, we propose a novel self auditing agentic retrieval augmented reasoning framework where intrusion detection is treated as a multi-hop process executed by collaborative agents on the logs, network telemetry and threat intelligence. We introduce multimodal embeddings to normalize different security data sources, retrieval-augmented generation to conduct evidence based reasoning, and a self auditing component to critically inspect the intermediate inference steps, detect inconsistencies and reduce adversarial influence. A dual-loop architecture comprising operational detection and perpetual validation provides robustness. Experimental studies on the large scale simulated enterprise data exhibit that our method increases detection accuracy by 17.8%, false positive rate by 26.4%, and cross-source correlation precision by 21.3% over the deep learning and RAG based IDS methods with a performance degradation of below 5% on the adversarial test-beds.
